Bug fix task, test-first. This temperature converter has a classic offset bug (it treats Fahrenheit-to-Celsius like a pure scale factor in one path). Put it in tconv.py verbatim:

def convert(value, src, dst):
    to_k = {'C': lambda v: v + 273.15, 'F': lambda v: v * 5/9 + 273.15, 'K': lambda v: v}
    from_k = {'C': lambda v: v - 273.15, 'F': lambda v: (v - 273.15) * 9/5 + 32, 'K': lambda v: v}
    return from_k[dst](to_k[src](value))

Write failing pytest cases first: convert(32, 'F', 'C') == 0 within 1e-9, convert(212, 'F', 'C') == 100, convert(-40, 'F', 'C') == -40, round-trip property convert(convert(x, 'C', 'F'), 'F', 'C') == x for 100 random values. Confirm they fail, fix only the buggy lambda, and also add delta-temperature support convert_delta(value, src, dst) where a 9 F change equals a 5 C change (no offset). Finish with everything green.

